WEBVTT

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.600
Pretty, huh?

00:01:58.960 --> 00:01:59.930
Yeah.

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.330
Hiroko Kageyama...

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.530
So there was a time when she looked like this.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.070
An innocent smile, knowing no corruption...

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.410
Everything around her is filled to overflowing with happiness,

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.940
...blessing that beauty.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.980
Fujisaki, you like sour women past their prime, because you're warped.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.160
If I like her, it's the young Hiroko I like.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:27.920
Not the sour one.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:35.430
Ah-choo!

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:52.980
This is likely the first time you've attended such a gathering, so try not to make any blunders.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.250
Yes, Ma'am.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:56.750
Well, let's go...

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.280
...to this false ceremony.

00:03:11.440 --> 00:03:16.000
A "living funeral" means having a funeral even though the person's not dead?

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.440
For the sake of saying farewell to people he had relationships with while he's still alive.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:24.470
What sort of person is Mr. Yuki?

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:28.350
He's the man who had Heaven's Gate built too, right?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:32.760
He was its largest sponsor as well as its founder.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:37.820
Now he's become the leader of Mitleid, and is pushing ahead with the sky cleansing.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:45.430
But I suppose his true role is as a fixer who possesses a hidden influence over this world.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:51.110
He seldom makes an appearance, so be sure to get a good look...

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:54.270
...at what sort of thing a monster from the previous century is.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.660
That was a tremendous sense of malice.

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.430
Nobody else noticed, huh?

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.510
What was concealed on the other side of that altar...

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:27.410
was probably his Special Forces, adopted and trained from childhood.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:29.850
The old gentleman was also a stand-in.

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.420
A stand-in?

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.250
He's a double.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:40.310
Thank you for taking time from your busy schedule today.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.460
Not at all.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.660
The Chairman says he will personally see you afterwards.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.100
This time it will be the real one.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:54.340
Very well.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:57.500
I'll see you presently.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.780
You're here, are you?

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.320
Who is that man?

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.750
Hayato Kazamatsuri, the Chairman's confidant.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:19.860
He's been entrusted with the military affiliate Equus.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:22.860
He's young, but he's quite sharp.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:28.800
A monster from the previous century, huh?

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:32.040
I think if I had to pick though, I'd say that more than the old man,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.140
...Little Hiroko is the monster.

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.680
Ah-choo!

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.720
I'm just gonna go wash up!

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:49.220
What's wrong with Fuko?

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.230
It got stronger again!

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.390
She said Special Forces, right?

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.130
Where?

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:12.350
Madoka, are you all right?

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.580
Tatsuya!

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:24.420
Looks like he came to.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.900
Should I call the doctor?

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:38.270
No...

00:06:38.540 --> 00:06:43.010
Seems it was just a slight attack of anemia. If he rests a bit...

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:45.140
I hope that's it.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.140
Well, then...

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:50.880
If you need anything...

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.890
We're very sorry about this.

00:07:01.100 --> 00:07:03.330
How long was I...

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:04.630
Just very briefly.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.370
How come...

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:10.670
That sense of malice from before was amplified by Dynamis.

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:15.610
It's creepy though.

00:07:16.480 --> 00:07:19.080
A stronghold of evil where a monster dwells, huh?

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:24.810
These are extremely strict precautions.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:30.990
That's because, as you are aware, there are those who seek to take the Chairman's life.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.960
Normally, we keep his location absolutely unknown,

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:40.790
...but today it wasn't an option for him to be absent.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.370
I see.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.780
It's been a very long time.

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:06.900
Little Hiroko... It would be rude if I called you that, eh?

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:10.130
Countess of Werdenberg...

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:13.260
No, Little Hiroko is just fine.

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:17.330
I was the godparent who gave this child her name.

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.810
And I got leaked on a lot when I held her as a baby.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.720
Not again...

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:29.920
How many years has it been?

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:34.260
Twenty years, since it was before I left for my post over there.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:40.760
When you were a child, you would often visit to spend the night with your family.

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:45.590
The time I spent here was so much fun.

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.570
I feel like it was the happiest time of my life.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:55.080
Even after that, your life must have been one to make others envious.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.880
Isn't that so?

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.540
Until Twin X, at least.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:05.080
I died at that time.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.360
What is that object set in the alcove?

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:18.060
It's a tablet inscribed with the world's oldest story, "The Epic of Gilgamesh."

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:24.510
There was a king, part human, part god, of the Mesopotamian city of Uruk.

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.250
His name was Gilgamesh.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:33.150
After many adventures, he set out upon a journey of great hardship, seeking immortality.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.980
I wonder if he found eternal life?

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:42.820
Gilgamesh, the beasts who are his revived form.

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:45.900
If you think about it, that lot is to be pitied.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:51.560
Coaxed by a great fool, reduced to tools of terrorism...

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.270
The legendary king is likely turning in his grave.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.670
This is Reiko, whom I've adopted as a daughter.

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:14.750
What is Tatsuya's condition?

00:10:17.160 --> 00:10:19.430
They said it's nothing serious.

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:21.960
I'm sorry for the nuisance to you.

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:27.730
I've been told that boy is a clone, of Enkidu.

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:31.040
Yes...

00:10:31.910 --> 00:10:34.430
It wasn't you who bore him though, was it?

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:41.290
The woman who was Enkidu's wife did, in order to prove her husband innocent of the crime.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:43.980
Using him to absolve himself, eh?

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:49.920
Now you're keeping him with you and making him fight Gilgamesh.

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.330
I wonder if you're not the same as the boy's mother?

00:10:57.030 --> 00:11:03.170
Little Hiroko, you believe in his innocence, the innocence of the first man you ever loved.

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.940
And in your own way, you're trying to settle things.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.540
Am I right?

00:11:15.950 --> 00:11:17.720
You may be so.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:20.980
Then that boy deserves to be pitied.

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:25.000
Right? Don't you think so?

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:28.600
I don't know. I'm just a dummy.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:33.370
Frankly, having amateurs hanging around getting in our way is an annoyance.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:36.740
That said, the children's Dynamis shouldn't go to waste.

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:40.870
Won't you place those children in our keeping?

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:45.380
How about it? Will you think about it?

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:50.720
No, I intend to carry through to the end in my own way.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:56.220
And also, because we're a family.

00:11:57.800 --> 00:12:00.160
You'd be well advised not to underestimate us.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:07.070
That's enough talk for now.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:09.900
Here, eat these while they're still cold.

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.400
Thank you.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:16.880
I brought these pomegranate trees from Heaven's Gate.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.480
I even changed the soil, so the seeds are sweet too.

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.800
Now I feel better.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:44.040
I never have this problem when he's not around though.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:13.630
Don't eat me! Oink, oink!

00:13:23.710 --> 00:13:25.740
Watch out that you don't get too close.

00:13:26.650 --> 00:13:29.150
They're docile ordinarily,

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:31.640
...but once they bite, they don't let go until they're dead.

00:13:32.390 --> 00:13:34.860
You're one of the kids from the Countess's place, right?

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:36.720
You have Dynamis.

00:13:37.300 --> 00:13:39.860
Mr. Kazamatsuri, wasn't it?

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:42.260
Right...

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:46.070
I remember this sense of malice.

00:13:47.170 --> 00:13:49.730
The last time we fought Gilgamesh...

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:55.470
They fled that time, upon feeling this presence.

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:59.380
That's because we taught them a good lesson once.

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:02.710
You're not the only ones who are fighting them.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.830
I hear you sneaked into our company's reference room.

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:10.260
What were you trying to do?

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:14.190
We thought it was about time we knew about ourselves.

00:14:15.570 --> 00:14:19.660
About Orga? And about Dynamis?

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:24.140
The Countess won't tell you?

00:14:25.880 --> 00:14:27.900
She just evades all our questions.

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:31.450
If that's the case, then shall I tell you?

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:35.050
And what might it be that you're saying you'll tell him?

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.650
Just the truth.

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:47.820
The fact is, I just returned from a trip to Uruk, to gather Lapis Warka, you see.

00:14:50.000 --> 00:14:53.060
That place, even now, is in a hellish state.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:58.600
Unlike myself, you're an involved party.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.880
It would probably be best if you told them.

00:15:04.050 --> 00:15:07.950
If you don't, those children will leave you.

00:15:10.790 --> 00:15:15.890
In any case, this is nothing for me to worry about.

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:26.900
Those things you told me before... Were they true?

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:28.810
Yeah.

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:32.640
You said Fujisaki was in a juvenile treatment center, right?

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:36.100
I can't imagine Isamu creating any mischief or anything.

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:41.780
I definitely think it was because he snapped after somebody did something to him.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:44.550
I remember Fuko was...

00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:49.820
She said she grew up in that kind of place from as early as she can remember.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:52.520
Were they making her work?

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.570
I don't know.

00:15:55.570 --> 00:16:00.800
Not asking too much about each other is our rule for living together.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:06.410
As for me, I'm the fortunate one.

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:12.080
I was living with my mother, and I was pretty happy, considering.

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:21.860
How do you feel?

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.660
I'm fine now.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:26.800
To just fall over like that, you're a real feeb.

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:28.670
You shouldn't talk.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:31.360
What do you think Fu here was doing?

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:37.410
She was at the catering table, munching away all by herself.

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:40.750
If it were me, you know, I'd think to eat together with everyone.

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.740
Yeah, well, I was hungry!

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:46.420
If you don't watch it, you'll turn into a pig!

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.590
Oink-oink-oink!

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:50.720
We'll call you Oinker instead of Fu!

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:54.320
Oink-oink-oink-oi-oi-oi-oink... ah-choo!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.570
That's gross!

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:02.900
You look like you're fine now.

00:17:13.080 --> 00:17:16.510
I'm sorry I made such a blunder.

00:17:16.510 --> 00:17:18.220
That's fine.

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.820
You're all hungry, aren't you? Let's eat.

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.180
Let's eat.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.990
Fu, that means you too.

00:17:27.990 --> 00:17:29.720
I don't need any.

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.260
Gilgamesh?!

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:08.200
Yeah.

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:11.470
Wait, we're in the middle of a meal.

00:18:11.470 --> 00:18:13.830
Those creatures have a clear objective.

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:23.650
And besides, having amateurs like you hanging around getting in the way...

00:18:23.650 --> 00:18:25.210
...would be an annoyance, right?

00:18:26.050 --> 00:18:30.080
Since there are a large number of trained professionals here...

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:35.190
Well, let's accept the "honor" of watching them at work.

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:07.590
Just now, was that...

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:09.130
Dynamis.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:10.090
No way...

00:19:10.760 --> 00:19:12.560
But all of us are here.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:18.130
No question, that was Dynamis.

00:19:45.160 --> 00:19:48.620
No, it's all right. It's the Orga people I told you about.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.570
Where are Gilgamesh?

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:54.530
They got away from us. That'll be an upcoming task to pursue.

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.110
Where are the Special Forces people?

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.910
They've already withdrawn.

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:01.150
They're quick!

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:04.820
Or you could say they're kinda like cockroaches.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:10.450
They are indeed cockroaches. Their name is even Blattaria.

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:12.010
Blattaria?

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:20.860
With your indispensable Chairman gone, isn't it all for naught?

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:26.600
He has fulfilled his duties. He'll be promoted two ranks posthumously.

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:29.270
It can't be... A double!

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:36.270
Did you honestly believe the Chairman himself was here today?

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:40.950
Oh, this is good.

00:20:40.950 --> 00:20:44.410
I just thought you were joining us in the performance.

00:20:51.000 --> 00:20:55.130
That's why I told you, don't underestimate us.

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:07.670
The girl from before...

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:23.660
The one who used Dynamis was you, wasn't it?

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:29.900
I don't know. I'm just a dummy.

00:23:25.180 --> 00:23:27.480
Jeez, I wonder what this is from?

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:29.250
This is the worst.

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:31.190
I'm short on Dynamis.

00:23:31.190 --> 00:23:32.290
That's the blue sky?

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:34.860
Right, it all depends on Little Hiroko's mood.

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:37.560
They told us we could use any method we want...

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.900
Who cares what color the sky is?

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:41.900
What do you mean, what?

00:23:41.900 --> 00:23:42.830
Hey, give me some!

00:23:42.830 --> 00:23:45.370
Jerk! This kind of thing's just a friendly greeting, you know!

00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:46.070
How come?

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:47.040
It feels good, you know.

00:23:47.040 --> 00:23:48.340
I'm going home.

00:23:48.340 --> 00:23:48.940
You got a problem with it?

00:23:48.940 --> 00:23:49.940
What?!

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:50.570
What's the problem?

00:23:50.570 --> 00:23:51.510
Jeez!

00:23:51.510 --> 00:23:53.440
I got a nosebleed.
